{
  "slug": "indian-company-drafting",
  "name": "Indian Company Drafting",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "For every company-law litigator, insolvency professional, and corporate counsel practising before India's company-law tribunals — every National Company Law Tribunal bench across India and the National Company Law Appellate Tribunal (Principal Bench and Chennai Bench) — this open-source Claude Code plugin standardises Companies Act and IBC drafting. Case-config-aware: forum, share-capital structure, board composition, alleged-oppression acts, scheme terms, capital-reduction arithmetic, strike-off history, investigation grounds, operational-debt particulars, corporate-applicant financial distress, and the NCLT order under appeal are user-supplied. Battle-tested for Sections 241 / 242 / 244 (oppression and mismanagement), Section 245 (class action), Sections 230-232 (compromise / arrangement / amalgamation / scheme), Section 66 (reduction of share capital), Section 252 (revival of a struck-off company), Section 213 (investigation into the affairs of a company), IBC Section 9 (operational-creditor CIRP application), IBC Section 10 (corporate-applicant self-initiation), Companies Act Section 421 (NCLAT appeal from NCLT order), and IBC Section 61 (NCLAT appeal from NCLT order under the IBC). Six-agent drafting pipeline + shared company drafting base with the Companies Act 2013, IBC 2016, NCLT Rules 2016, NCLAT Rules 2016, IBBI Regulations, Secretarial Standards SS-1 / SS-2, Companies (Compromises, Arrangements and Amalgamations) Rules 2016, Companies (Inspection, Investigation and Inquiry) Rules 2014, BNSS 2023, and BSA 2023 encoded. Companies Act 1956 → 2013 transition discipline encoded in the Verifier. The finished product is a Tribunal-ready petition or appeal the chamber can lodge at the NCLT or NCLAT Registry the same day.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **12 skills** and **6 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (12): `_company_drafting_base` (Universal Indian company-law tribunal pleading skeleton), `_drafting_common` (Shared reference for all 10 banking / financial-recovery / insolvency drafting skills), `ibc-section-10-corporate-applicant-draft` (Draft an Application under Section 10 of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code 2016 by a Corporate Applicant /…), `ibc-section-9-operational-creditor-application-draft` (Draft an Application under Section 9 of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code 2016 by an Operational Creditor for…), `nclat-appeal-section-421-draft` (Draft a Memorandum of Appeal before the National Company Law Appellate Tribunal under Section 421 of the Companies…), `nclat-appeal-section-61-ibc-draft` (Draft a Memorandum of Appeal before the National Company Law Appellate Tribunal under Section 61 of the Insolvency…), `nclt-scheme-of-arrangement-draft` (Draft a Scheme of Arrangement / Compromise / Amalgamation / Merger / Demerger Application before the National Company…), `nclt-section-213-investigation-draft` (Draft an Application before the National Company Law Tribunal under Section 213 of the Companies Act 2013 read…), and 4 more\n- **Agents** (6): `drafter` (Third agent in the Indian company-law tribunal drafting pipeline), `format` (Second agent in the Indian company-law tribunal drafting pipeline), `overseer` (Sixth and final agent in the Indian company-law tribunal drafting pipeline), `reader` (First agent in the Indian company-law tribunal drafting pipeline), `refiner` (Fifth agent in the Indian company-law tribunal drafting pipeline), `verifier` (Fourth agent in the Indian company-law tribunal drafting pipeline)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install indian-company-drafting@claude-community` from `Wolfgangrush/indian-company-drafting`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
